Review this Kibana route for OAS compliance. The route was first added in 9.2.0 and is experimental. The PR adds a new 'reasoning_level' property in 9.6.0:

```typescript
// server/routes/conversations.ts
router.versioned.post({
  path: '/api/agent_builder/conversations',
  summary: 'Create a conversation',
  description: 'Create a new agent conversation.',
  options: {
    tags: ['access:agentBuilder', 'oas-tag:Agent builder'],
    availability: {
      stability: 'experimental',
      since: '9.2.0',
    },
  },
})
.addVersion(
  {
    version: '2023-10-31',
    validate: {
      request: {
        body: schema.object({
          title: schema.string({
            meta: { description: 'The conversation title.' },
          }),
          reasoning_level: schema.maybe(
            schema.oneOf(
              [schema.literal('low'), schema.literal('medium'), schema.literal('high')],
              {
                meta: {
                  description: 'Reasoning effort level for the LLM.',
                },
              }
            )
          ),
        }),
      },
    },
    options: {
      oasOperationObject: () => path.join(__dirname, 'examples/conversations_create.yaml'),
    },
  },
  handler
)
```

